00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,240
Zero.

76
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,080
Yes, that's zero.

77
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:17,880
So, this says that when you have that utility function,

78
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,960
the expected value maximization utility function,

79
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:22,000
then you have no risk aversion.

80
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,520
All right, that makes sense.

