00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:09,640
So, this says that when the insurance is actually fair,

263
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,080
then everyone is gonna wanna buy

264
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,660
$1,000 worth of insurance.

265
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,280
All right, and that's interesting,

266
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:18,880
because the good outcome is $1,000.

267
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:21,600
Then people also want $1,000 worth of insurance

268
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,600
at the actually fair rate.

269
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:26,240
So, in other words, what this winds up saying

270
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:29,360
is that if people are risk averse,

271
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:30,840
so people are risk averse,

272
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:33,960
and they can get actually fair insurance,

273
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:37,600
they want to have absolute certainty about their income.

274
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,000
And so, how can you get absolute certainty

275
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,500
with actually fair insurance?

276
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:46,160
You just make income the same in both periods.

277
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,960
So, you buy enough insurance

278
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:51,800
so that after subtracting out the premiums,

279
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:53,120
your income in both periods are equal,

280
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,040
and it's actually fair.

281
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,040
This means that you're just going to have

282
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,200
the average in every period, in every situation.

283
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,440
So, since you have $1,000 with a 0.6 chance,

284
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,760
zero with a 0.4,

285
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,680
this means that you buy enough insurance

286
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,860
so you have 600 in every period.

287
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,720
In other words, if you're risk averse

288
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,960
and you can get rid of your risk for sure,

289
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,480
at no additional cost,

290
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:19,300
other than that you have to pay the actually fair amount,

291
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:20,520
what do you opt for?

292
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:23,400
A life of perfect certainty and perfect mediocrity,

293
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:26,240
where you get rid of all upside and downside risk

294
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:29,920
by just getting a flat amount of income in every scenario.

295
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:34,160
Okay, and then you can also go and show

296
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:36,800
that if theta, or rather, if X is,

297
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:39,620
that if X is actually greater than one,

298
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:42,040
so the insurance is not actually really fair,

299
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:45,240
then even risk averse agents don't fully insure.

300
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,120
So you can show that you can prove that as well.

301
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,840
So in other words, if X is, say, 1.1,

302
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:54,240
then you cannot get rid of all risk for no cost,

303
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,480
and this says that then even risk averse people

304
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,280
will live with some uncertainty.

305
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:01,820
And in fact, if X were big enough,

306
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:04,360
you could get risk averse people to sell insurance.

307
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,720
So if you had a really high price for insurance

308
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,140
in a barter market,

309
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:11,760
then very risk averse people would go and sell insurance,

310
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,760
and who would the risk averse people sell their insurance to?

311
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,800
Even more risk averse people.

312
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:20,040
Yes, so that's totally possible.

313
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:26,280
So, questions about problems like this?

314
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:31,600
All right, and now then let's move on

315
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,440
to efficiency implications

316
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,480
of symmetric or perfect information.

